Source: zl-autodev
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: ZealLab LLC <info@zeallab.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: zl-autodev
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, zl-tools, git, cron | cron-daemon
Recommends: xdg-utils
Suggests: ollama
Description: ZealLab AutoDev - scheduled autonomous AI development loops
 Registers local git repositories for unattended, scheduled development by an
 AI coding agent. Each run builds one backlog item, runs the project's gates
 and a review, then commits locally or rolls back. Nothing is ever pushed.
 .
 Managed from a local web dashboard (http://localhost:7777) and scheduled
 through the user's crontab. Invoked as "zl autodev".
 .
 Works with Claude Code and the Codex CLI (subscription logins), Ollama and
 the AntiGravity CLI. Those tools are not installed by this package.
